.TH NZBTUI 1 "November 2026" "nzbtui 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nzbtui \- standalone terminal Usenet client built with Ratatui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nzbtui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nzbtui
is a standalone Rust TUI Usenet client with direct Newznab indexer search,
multi-connection TLS NNTP downloading with priority backup fallback, yEnc
decoding, on-demand PAR2 verification/repair, and archive extraction.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternate JSON configuration file (default: \fI~/.config/nzbtui/config.json\fR).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-import " " \fINZB_FILE\fR
Immediately enqueue one or more local .nzb files on startup. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-config\-path
Print the default configuration file path and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nzbtui/config.json
User configuration (providers, indexers, download paths, post-processing). Saved with mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nzbtui/history.json
Completed and failed download history.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR par2 (1),
.BR 7z (1),
.BR unrar (1),
.BR unzip (1)
